  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will learn how to write terms that include rational exponents as radicals and vice versa.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Simplify radical expressions with even and odd indexes. </item>
  <item> Rewrite expressions with rational exponents as roots. </item>
  <item> Use properties for exponents with rational exponents.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item>5.2.1: Perfect Squares Revisited</item>
  <item>5.2.2: The nth Root
    <list>
      <item> 5.2.2: Self Check  </item>
      <item> 5.2.2: Additional Resources </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>5.2.3: Radicals and Rational Exponents 
    <list>
      <item> 5.2.3: Self Check  </item>
      <item> 5.2.3: Additional Resources </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>5.2.4: Properties of Exponents with Rationals </item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 5.2.5: Practice </item>
  <item> 5.2.6: Lesson Summary </item>
</list></section>
</content>
